{"id":"n-20261026-o2qwg9","category":"finance","display_title":"Wall Street Investors Shift to ETFs","display_title_he":"משקיעי וול סטריט עוברים לקרנות סל","short_summary":"As Wall Street deals with mounting costs and uncertainties surrounding artificial intelligence, investors are abandoning individual stocks in record numbers and pouring billions into thematic exchange-traded funds.","english_level":"C1","words":602,"reading_time":4,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Wall_Street_bubbles_-_Always_the_same_-_Keppler_1901.jpg/960px-Wall_Street_bubbles_-_Always_the_same_-_Keppler_1901.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"Udo Keppler · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wall_Street_bubbles_-_Always_the_same_-_Keppler_1901.jpg"},"sources":[{"name":"Globes","domain":"globes.co.il","url":"https://www.globes.co.il/news/article.aspx?did=1001560662","title":"המשקיעים בורחים ממניות בודדות - אבל מסתערים על הקרנות האלו","published_at":"2026-10-25T13:52:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-25T13:52:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-26T06:15:07.130Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Wall Street's romantic entanglement with artificial intelligence has recently encountered a harsh economic reality. Although investors poured vast amounts of capital into technology equities throughout 2026, mounting borrowing costs, massive commitments toward establishing data centers, and persistent questions regarding the timeline for investment returns have pushed traders to look for an escape hatch. Yet, the financial landscape remains far from one-dimensional. While market participants abandon specific single stocks, they are aggressively rushing into targeted exchange-traded funds to mitigate risk.","Fresh data from Bank of America highlights the magnitude of this turbulence. According to a report published by strategist Jill Carey Hall, clients of the second-largest bank in the United States sold a record-shattering fourteen point eight billion dollars worth of individual equities in just a single week. This selling wave crossed virtually every investment category, extending from institutional clients and hedge funds down to retail investors. The damage was not restricted exclusively to the technology sector; the industrial sector simultaneously recorded its twelfth consecutive week of capital outflows, signaling a broader retreat from companies tied to wider economic expansion.","Despite this massive liquidation, capital did not leave the broader market entirely; it merely transformed its vehicle. While individual shares absorbed heavy blows, technology funds attracted eighteen point eight billion dollars during that exact same week, marking their highest influx of capital since July. This stark contrast illustrates how investors hesitate to pick individual winning stocks manually and instead prefer distributing their exposure through pooled index vehicles.","Simultaneously, the asset management industry has recognized this intense market appetite and responded with a flood of new product offerings. Since the beginning of 2026, no fewer than seventy-three thematic exchange-traded funds have debuted in the United States, representing an eighty-seven percent surge compared to the previous year. Aniket Ullal, head of exchange-traded fund research and analytics at CFRA Research, explained to MarketWatch that investors are actively trying to dissect the artificial intelligence theme into granular components to understand its underlying structure.","This trend has catalyzed the creation of exceptionally specialized financial products. Offerings now range from funds focusing on robotics and humanoid machines to portfolios tracking the ecosystems of artificial intelligence laboratories, including giants like OpenAI, Google, and Meta, alongside cybersecurity and space exploration funds. Brian Armour, a fund research director at Morningstar, observed that artificial intelligence remains the dominant market motif, but the year 2026 has introduced refined instruments that distill this exposure with greater precision. For professional portfolio managers, deciphering the subsequent phase of this technological revolution remains paramount. JJ Jacobs, head of United States equity exchange-traded funds at BlackRock, described it as one of the defining generational themes. Alongside gross domestic product growth and prevailing interest rates, artificial intelligence stands as a primary market driver, with the next logical frontier involving its integration into the physical world.","This continuous hunt for industrial bottlenecks has likewise fostered creative financial issuances, including specialized funds centered on memory chips or photonics, which utilize laser light rather than traditional copper wiring inside data centers. Matthew Tuttle, chief executive officer of Tuttle Capital Management, summarized the prevailing corporate mindset by noting that everyone is currently trying to invent the next big financial hit. Nonetheless, analysts caution that mass migration into niche funds or defensive sectors like energy, consumer staples, and healthcare harbors entirely novel risks. Should investors flee expensive technology shares solely to crowd into popular alternative safe havens, those very substitutes risk becoming inflated bubbles of their own. A bubble within a bubble can easily materialize when participants confuse a popular hiding place with genuine long-term value, leaving valuations exceptionally difficult to navigate before the next major market wave."],"facts":[{"fact":"In 2026, Wall Street's relationship with artificial intelligence faced pressure due to rising borrowing costs, massive data center commitments, and questions about return on investment.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"According to a Bank of America report by strategist Jill Carey Hall, bank clients sold a record $14.8 billion in individual stocks in a single week.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The industrial sector recorded its 12th consecutive week of outflows.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"While individual stocks suffered, technology funds attracted $18.8 billion in the exact same week, the highest inflow since July.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"In 2026, 73 thematic ETFs were launched in the US, an 87% increase compared to the previous year, approaching the 2021 peak of 90 launches.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"New niche funds focus on areas such as robotics, humanoid robots, AI labs ecosystems (OpenAI, Google, Meta), cybersecurity, space, memory chips, and photonics.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Analysts like Brian Armour from Morningstar and JJ Kinahan warn that shifting heavily into popular safe havens or thematic sub-sectors could create a bubble within a bubble.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Wall Street","lemma":"Wall Street","pos":"noun","he":"וול סטריט","name":"true"},{"text":"romantic entanglement","lemma":"romantic entanglement","pos":"noun","he":"רומן","name":false},{"text":"artificial intelligence","lemma":"artificial intelligence","pos":"noun","he":"בינה מלאכותית","name":false},{"text":"recently","lemma":"recently","pos":"adverb","he":"לאחרונה","name":false},{"text":"encounter","lemma":"encounter","pos":"verb","he":"נתקל","name":false},{"text":"harsh","lemma":"harsh","pos":"adjective","he":"קשה / לא נוח","name":false},{"text":"economic reality","lemma":"economic reality","pos":"noun","he":"מציאות כלכלית","name":false},{"text":"investor","lemma":"investor","pos":"noun","he":"משקיע","name":false},{"text":"pour","lemma":"pour","pos":"verb","he":"הזרימ","name":false},{"text":"vast amount","lemma":"vast amount","pos":"noun","he":"הון עתק","name":false},{"text":"capital","lemma":"capital","pos":"noun","he":"הון","name":false},{"text":"technology equity","lemma":"technology equity","pos":"noun","he":"מניות טכנולוגיה",